1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,120
In this video, we'll show you how to use the dashboards and analytics features to interpret

2
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:13,120
the results of your scan and begin taking steps to resolve any issues.

3
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:17,680
First, you can get a summary of your site's security posture by navigating to the overview

4
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:19,380
tab.

5
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:24,580
This contains various charts that give you a quick snapshot of how secure your site is.

6
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:29,520
If your scan is still running, these are updated in real time as more vulnerabilities are detected.

7
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:35,520
Next, go to the Issues tab to see a list of all security issues that have been identified

8
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:38,120
by the scan so far.

9
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:43,860
These are colour coded based on the estimated severity of the issues.

10
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:45,140
Issues are grouped by type.

11
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:51,680
You can expand each issue type to see all of the URLs where this issue is detected.

12
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:55,780
When faced with a large number of issues, you'll want to prioritise.

13
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:59,500
Use the buttons at the top of the list to apply filters so that only issues with a high severity

14
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:04,260
and certain confidence level are displayed.

15
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:08,260
The confidence level is determined by the inherent accuracy of the techniques used to detect each

16
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:10,260
type of issue.

17
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:15,040
Issues with a lower confidence level may require manual confirmation.

18
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:19,080
At this point, you might want to get more information about an issue.

19
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:23,700
Select one for URLs where reflected cross-site scripting was detected.

20
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:27,780
The advisory tab provides information to help you understand what the problem is and what

21
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:32,460
actions you can take to resolve the issue.

22
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:37,220
In some cases, you'll find links to the Web Security Academy, where you can find more information

23
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:41,220
and practise exploiting the issue yourself on a series of deliberately vulnerable websites.

24
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:53,980
At the bottom of the advisory information, where possible, you'll find issues mapped to vulnerability

25
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:54,980
classifications.

26
00:01:54,980 --> 00:02:03,740
Additional tabs display the evidence that Burp Scanner has found for the issue.

27
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:06,740
The type of evidence that is available depends on the issue type.

28
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:13,740
In this case, you can see tabs containing snippets of relevant HTTP requests and responses.

29
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:17,820
Open the request and notice the proof of concept payload that Burp Scanner sent to your site

30
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:20,100
is highlighted.

31
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:24,920
Open the response and observe that this payload was reflected in the returned HTML content,

32
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:30,500
potentially enabling an attacker to execute arbitrary JavaScript in another user's browser.

33
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:36,140
After manually reviewing a reported issue, you may decide that it is in fact a false positive.

34
00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:42,740
Once the scan has finished running, select any issue, then click mark as false positive.

35
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,820
For now, just accept the default setting.

36
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:54,740
You'll often want to report the results of your scan to other stakeholders who don't

37
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:57,920
have access to Burp Suite Enterprise Edition.

38
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:02,080
For example, you need to pass details of any findings to your development team so that they

39
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,340
can work on a fix.

40
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:07,580
Go back to the scan and open the Reporting and Logs tab.

41
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:12,240
Download a detailed report including high and medium severity issues with false positives

42
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,240
excluded.

43
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:18,160
Now you have a detailed scan report to share with the appropriate stakeholders to help secure

44
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,160
your web estate.

